{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-j1e-local-states","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:j1e-local-states","kind":"remark","title":"J^1E as the space of local states","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-irreducible-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group","tags":["jet-bundle","gauge-theory"],"text":"j1e-local-states.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"rem:j1e-local-states\"></a>\n<strong>Remark.</strong> <em>J^1E as the space of local states</em></p>\n<p>The jet bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^1 \\mathcal{S}</code> accommodates the local states. The substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> weights the classical gauge dynamics on the instanton connection to constitute the quantum field algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code>.</p>\n"}
